cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "p-hacking-skills: a specification-search audit and p-hacking benchmark for econometric designs"
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Bryce
version: 0.4.1
date-released: 2026-09-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/brycewang-stanford/p-hacking-skills"
abstract: >-
  A toolkit for studying p-hacking in design-based empirical economics: a
  specification-search engine that leaves a complete ledger, null-calibrated
  honest p-values for exhaustive and sequential searches, Stata / R / Python /
  StatsPAI runners over the same grid, a detection battery, and a benchmark
  for whether AI research agents p-hack. Intended for research and teaching
  about p-hacking, not for producing findings.
keywords:
  - p-hacking
  - specification search
  - multiverse analysis
  - research integrity
  - econometrics
  - AI agent evaluation
